    "durationMs": 112565,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL shortener is implemented and fully verified end-to-end.\n\n**What I built:**\n- **Stack**: Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21, Spring Data JPA, Flyway + PostgreSQL. Added the missing deps to `pom.xml` (plus `spring-boot-maven-plugin` so the jar is executable).\n- **Schema**: Flyway migration `V1__init.sql` creates the `links` table (unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`).\n- **API** (`bench.app` package): `POST /links` (201, generated or custom code; 409 on duplicate; 422 on malformed JSON / bad URL / bad code), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`), `GET /links/{code}`, and `GET /r/{code}` (302 with the stored URL verbatim in `Location`, one atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1` per request).\n- **Config**: `start.sh` converts `DATABASE_URL` (postgresql:// → jdbc:postgresql://) into `SPRING_DATASOURCE_*` env vars and runs the prebuilt `target/app.jar` in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000; Flyway applies pending migrations at boot. No credentials hard-coded; README documents startup.\n\n**Verified via HTTP tests**: all happy paths, duplicate → 409, 11 validation cases → 422, unknown codes → 404, URL/code boundary values (4 and 20 chars accepted, 3/21 rejected). After a server restart, all links and click counts survived, redirects kept incrementing correctly, and Flyway reported the schema already up to date. Test server is stopped, so port 8000 is free for the real run."
